# Constraint Model

DND-1.2 defines content constraints and domain types in `@dndgem/core`.
DND-1.3 implements validity evaluation and scoring in Core (`evaluateItemPlacement`, `evaluateLayout`).
DND-1.4 selects layouts via `solveLayout` using that evaluator (ADR-0010).

- Prefer renderer-agnostic vocabulary over HTML/CSS semantics in core.
- Keep geometric bounds, minUseful*, and preferred* semantically distinct.
- Validity states and scoring belong in core, not in React components.
- Do not invent persistence I/O early; layout shapes include `schemaVersion`.
- Preferred dimensions affect score/reasons only — never validity alone.
- Hard geometric violations → INVALID; usefulness misses (hard OK) → DEGRADED.
- Solver candidates must be bounded and deterministic; do not duplicate the validity engine.
